# config/Kconfig.ota — Over-The-Air firmware update configuration
#
# OTA slot size limit.  Signature enforcement is
# OTA_SIG_MANDATORY (config/Kconfig.security; the scheme is Ed25519, the
# only one implemented).  The anti-rollback floors (BOOTMETA
# min_fw_version, min_sec_epoch) are always on; where the epoch floor is
# also held is OTA_FLOOR_* (config/Kconfig.security, next to TPM).

menu "OTA Firmware Updates"
config OTA_MAX_IMAGE_SIZE_MB
    int "Maximum OTA image size (MiB)"
    range 1 64
    default 8
    help
      Hard limit on firmware image size accepted by the OTA receiver.
      Images larger than this are rejected before writing to FAT.
      This is the ONLY size ceiling in the OTA path (crates/core/ota's
      `OTA_MAX_IMAGE_SIZE` reads this symbol via azos_limits, and
      `tools/ota_send.py` reads the same `.config` this expands to, so
      neither can drift from it). Secure boot verification used to carry
      a second, smaller, disconnected ceiling (a 2 MiB `.bss` buffer to
      hold a whole image); that buffer is gone as of 2026-09-26 (U09-14)
      now that verification streams the hash instead of buffering the
      image, so raising this value costs no extra `.bss`.

      Cost: none (+0 B of RAM measured for 8 -> 9 and -> 16 MiB, both ISAs).
endmenu # OTA Firmware Updates
